  "summary": "47 pass, 1 flag, 1 reject across 49 non-organization entities. The D-Wave Clarity and S-4 roadmap documents correctly remain partial: the PDF has omitted dated solver and Leap items, a 2025+ line, and undated gate-model phases, while the S-4 has additional forward-looking content. The Advantage2 outcome is correctly partially_met: D-Wave still expected 7,000 qubits in January 2024 and announced a 4,400+ qubit generally available system in May 2025. D-Wave revenue actuals correctly convert the 10-K tables from thousands to millions (8,758 to 8.758; 8,827 to 8.827; 24,587 to 24.587); no FY2022 actual was invented, gross-profit projections use the table row, and only positive Adjusted EBITDA projections were stored with their non-GAAP character disclosed. The Nature record preserves verbatim original and retraction sentences and records both the Delft affiliation and Microsoft Corporation Station-Q acknowledgement; it is flagged only because the schema labels the formal retraction notice peer_reviewed. Worst problem: Intel's no_delivery_found search was incomplete. Rejected id: out:intel-hist-next-chip-2024."
